CORE
main.c
--no-malloc-may-fail
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .*: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* b is reachable: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
pointer handling for concurrency is unsound
--
A pointer that a thread stores in a heap object reachable from a shared
pointer, read through a local copy and tested in a condition (which must not
filter the value set of the shared pointer).
